From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 20:25:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7915: add missing locking in
 mt7915_mac_sta_rc_work()

mt7915_mac_sta_rc_work() drops sta_poll_lock and then uses the station
and its vif to send rate control and SMPS updates to the firmware.
Station removal runs under dev->mt76.mutex and only takes the station
off sta_rc_list, so it doesn't wait for an update that is already in
progress and mac80211 can free the station while the work still uses
it.

Hold dev->mt76.mutex for the duration of the work, as
mt7996_mac_sta_rc_work() already does.
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 mt7915/mac.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/mt7915/mac.c b/mt7915/mac.c
index dcd44c05..b868cb26 100644
--- a/mt7915/mac.c
+++ b/mt7915/mac.c
@@ -1983,6 +1983,8 @@ void mt7915_mac_sta_rc_work(struct work_struct *work)
 	u32 changed;
 	LIST_HEAD(list);
 
+	mutex_lock(&dev->mt76.mutex);
+
 	spin_lock_bh(&dev->mt76.sta_poll_lock);
 	list_splice_init(&dev->sta_rc_list, &list);
 
@@ -2008,6 +2010,8 @@ void mt7915_mac_sta_rc_work(struct work_struct *work)
 	}
 
 	spin_unlock_bh(&dev->mt76.sta_poll_lock);
+
+	mutex_unlock(&dev->mt76.mutex);
 }
 
 void mt7915_mac_work(struct work_struct *work)
